Tue Nov 24 17:08:07 UTC 2026 - Egbert Eich <eich@suse.com>

- Update to version 0.1.10
  * Upgrade Notes
    - Application URLs now come from the supervisor application
      origin, separate from the gateway connection. Gateway-mediated
      application routing can be turned off with `enable_gateway_service_routing`
      (default `true`). Users of the app listener must replace
      `domain` with `base_url`, deploy matching gateway, driver and
      supervisor images, and recreate existing dedicated sandbox
      pods with the new supervisor image.
    - Repository references and links now point to `ai-openshell/openshell`
      after the repository transfer.
  * Bug Fixes
    - Sandboxed workloads can now set their own CPU affinity, nice
      value and resource limits, signal themselves and queue signals,
      like in a plain container. Calls targeting processes outside
      the workload's own thread group are still denied.
    - HTTP clients (including JSON-RPC and MCP) are now promptly
      notified when an upstream closes an idle connection. Proxy
      failures before a response starts now return `502 Bad Gateway`
      with a request ID.
    - Request inspection and authorization now use the protocol
      chosen by the matching route, so overlapping routes and RPC/MCP
      requests get the right decision.
    - Clients that cache DNS answers can open new connections after
      a policy DNS mapping expires; the destination is refreshed
      and re-checked before connecting.
    - Restarting a sandbox no longer sometimes marks it as `Error`
      (`ContainerExited`) while it is still starting.
    - On multi-replica gateways, attaching to a sandbox whose main
      process has finished no longer fails with `sandbox is not
      ready`.
    - Sandbox create/start/restart/delete operations no longer
      serialize across the whole fleet during SSH identity setup,
      and lock holders can no longer exhaust the gateway's database
      connections.
    - Application streams no longer close early when serving authority
      is renewed ahead of its deadline.
    - Gateway replicas can now reach each other on IPv6 clusters.
    - Transparent egress to an allowed IPv6 address no longer closes
      without a response.
    - Bundled SQLite updated to address RUSTSEC-2026-0459.
  * Features
    - Docker gateways can give new workspaces persistent `/sandbox`
      storage and update a stopped sandbox's image without changing
      its sandbox ID (requires sandbox updates to be enabled on the
      gateway; existing workspaces are unchanged).
    - Providers can mint and rotate GitHub App installation tokens
      with a defined repository and permission scope, so long-running
      workloads keep access without seeing the app's private key.
    - Workspace secrets allow storing a shared secret once and
      referencing it from the refresh settings of multiple providers.
      Disabled unless the gateway sets `enable_workspace_secrets`.
    - OAuth refresh providers accept `token_endpoint_auth_method=client_secret_basic`
      and `resource=<uri>`. Defaults are unchanged.
    - Credential `path_template` values can end in `/`, so one token
      can cover every method under an API path (e.g. `/bot{credential}/`).
    - AKS deployments can use Entra workload identity for external
      Azure PostgreSQL instead of a stored database password.
    - Gateway metrics can be sent to an OTLP collector by setting
      `enabled = true` under `[openshell.gateway.otlp.metrics]`.
      Prometheus scraping continues to work alongside it.
    - Gateway audit records now name the resources each change
      touched (workspaces, sandboxes, providers, credential keys,
      settings, draft policy chunks, exec channels, port forwards,
      SSH sessions), flag no-op and replayed changes, and include
      the error reason when a change fails. Set `capture_setting_values
      = true` or `capture_exec_command = true` under
      `[openshell.gateway.audit]` to also record setting values or
      exec arguments.
    - Policy DNS answers AAAA queries on IPv6-only supervisor
      namespaces (`policy_dns_ipv6_egress`, `auto` by default), and
      SSRF checks treat a NAT64 address as the embedded IPv4 address.
    - Network and HTTP events show the actual process behind each
      sandbox connection instead of pid 0.
    - Sandbox startup traces show the time spent connecting to the
      boundary as a separate span.

