Wed Nov 18 16:18:53 UTC 2026 - Egbert Eich <eich@suse.com>

- Update openshell to v0.1.9:
  These are the user-visible changes:
  * Breaking changes and upgrade notes
    - Go SDK moved: it now lives at `github.com/ai-openshell/sdk-go`.
      The old path has been deprecated since v0.1.8.
    - Network policy: wildcard endpoints no longer allow private
      IP literals by themselves.
    - Postgres migration: the gateway migration builds indexes that
      block table writes. On large deployments, plan the upgrade
      around that.
    - Middleware selectors: selectors can no longer include a port,
      and validation now rejects them if they do.
    - HTTP middleware: new streaming hooks were added. `EvaluateHttpRequest`
      and `HttpResponsePreReturn` are deprecated and will be removed
      in v0.2.0.
  * New features
    - Sandbox startup timeouts can be set by operators:
      `provisioning_repair_window_seconds`, `runtime_bootstrap_grace_seconds`
      and `sandbox_attach_request_timeout_seconds`.
    - New CLI flag `openshell sandbox create --timeout <SECONDS>`
      controls how long to wait for provisioning.
    - Workspace commands can print as a table, JSON or YAML with
      `-o/--output table|json|yaml`.
    - Request ID header: HTTP responses include `X-OpenShell-Request-ID`,
      which links to OCSF records and traces.
    - ServiceDiscovery service: a new `openshell.v1.ServiceDiscovery`
      service lets you discover service routes.
    - Supervisor placement: shared supervisors are spread evenly
      across gateway replicas, with new placement metrics.
    - Delete records: gateway delete records now say which workspace
      and resource were deleted.
    - Grafana: a monitoring mixin provides operational dashboards.
  * Bug fixes
    - Long-running sandboxes no longer exit when the connection
      drops a second or later time.
    - Dedicated supervisors shut down cleanly within 8 seconds of
      SIGTERM.
    - Idle `exec` sessions no longer block new control connections.
    - Stopped sandboxes keep their state when driver updates arrive
      late.
    - Multi-replica gateways free the memory of deleted sandboxes.
    - Gateway and driver logs only use ANSI colors when writing to
      a terminal.
    - The TUI workspace shortcut cycles through the actual workspaces.
    - `rule history` shows the full timestamp.
    - Security updates: russh 0.65.1, the hickory-proto DNS parser
      and rustix memory-safety patches.
  * Other
    - Security docs now cover L7 audit mode and sandbox runtime
      protections in more depth.
    - The rest is internal: more end-to-end, CDI (Docker/Podman)
      and Jaeger trace tests, development process tooling, and
      dependency updates.

