Wed Nov 11 09:20:20 UTC 2026 - Matthias Eckermann <mge@suse.com>

- Updated to 0.1.8.
  * Breaking changes:
    - Credential placement is stricter: static provider credentials are
      now only injected into the Authorization header or an explicit
      body/WebSocket rewrite. If you use custom headers, query parameters
      or path slots, your policy must now declare where the credential goes.
    - WebSockets need explicit config: REST endpoints now reject HTTP upgrade
      requests with 403. WebSocket traffic needs its own protocol and rules
      in the policy.
    - Symlinks in writable workspaces can block launch: a sandbox won't
      start if a filesystem policy path goes through a symlink in a writable
      workspace.
  * SDK changes:
    - Go: move from github.com/NVIDIA/OpenShell/sdk/go to
      github.com/ai-openshell/sdk-go. The Go SDK now shares oidc_token.json
      with the CLI, so run openshell gateway login once.
    - Python: still pip install openshell, but it's now published from a
      separate repo.
  * User visible changes:
    - Stability: deleted sandboxes no longer leak memory, so repeated
      create/delete cycles no longer end in an OOM kill.
    - CLI:
      - openshell sandbox download now works on busybox-based images.
      - policy update --add-endpoint accepts allow-encoded-slash.
      - status --gateway <name> exits non-zero for unknown gateways.
      - Expired OIDC client-credentials tokens are renewed automatically if
        OPENSHELL_OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET is set.
      - TUI: the policy viewer shows the actual allowed/denied MCP tool names
        instead of wildcard patterns.
    - SDKs:
      - TypeScript: forward().close() now revokes the SSH forward token.
      - Go: falls back to the system-wide active gateway and sets up Listen
        tunnels in parallel.
      - Python: new optional delete_timeout_seconds.
  * New features
    - Tracing: the CLI passes TRACEPARENT/TRACESTATE on to the gateway, so CI
      pipeline traces can be linked to it.
    - Security warnings: you now get a warning when allow_unauthenticated_users
      is enabled, and when Docker Engine is older than 28.0.

